+++ b/sandbox-agent/docs/content/docs/deploy/pryx.mdx
@@ -0,0 +1,30 @@
+---
+title: "pryx"
+description: "Use a warmed sandbox-agent template on your pryx fleet."
+---
+
+Build and release the template from the pryx repository, then prepare it on the container tier:
+
+```sh
+pryx template create sandbox-agent
+```
+
+```typescript
+import { Pryx } from "@cubepals/pryx";
+import { SandboxAgent } from "sandbox-agent";
+import { pryx } from "sandbox-agent/pryx";
+
+const client = new Pryx({ url: process.env.PRYX_API_URL!, key: process.env.PRYX_API_KEY! });
+const agent = await SandboxAgent.start({ sandbox: pryx(client, {
+  key: crypto.randomUUID(), template: "sandbox-agent",
+}) });
+const result = await agent.runProcess({ command: "sh", args: ["-c", "echo hello"], cwd: "/data" });
+await agent.destroySandbox();
+```
+
+The key stays in the service closure. Use a durable creation key when recovering an uncertain
+create response. Reconnect wakes the existing sandbox; pause preserves data and destroy removes
+it. The server uses private control ingress, so run this service on the fleet's allowed control
+network. The warmed image contains the server; no mutable installer is downloaded at boot.
+An explicit image and server port may be selected instead of a template. Images require a
+container-tier node; pryx's host policy remains authoritative.
